From daf0898e4264894a392474660b386987dea030d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: user <user@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:57:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): hold message window while transcript is scrolled up

The sync store keeps a window of the last 100 messages per session and evicts the oldest from the top on every new message. For a reader who has scrolled the history up this removes rows above the viewport, so every remaining message shifts up and the visible text jumps forward by the evicted height on each agent message. Register a reader-at-bottom gate from the session route: while the reader is away from the bottom the window only grows, and everything accumulated above it is dropped in one pass once they return to the bottom, where the drop is off-screen.
---
